    "title": "South Korean President Lee Jae Myung Visits China Amidst Regional Tensions",
    "text": "• South Korean President Lee Jae Myung arrived in China on Sunday for a four-day visit.\n• This is Lee's first visit to China since taking office in June.\n• The visit occurs amid heightened tensions between China and Japan over Taiwan.\n• Lee will meet with Chinese President Xi Jinping, their second meeting in two months.\n• Lee gave an interview to China's state broadcaster CCTV, stating his government cares about relations between Beijing and Seoul.\n• Lee assured that South Korea respects the “One-China” policy regarding Taiwan.\n• Lee said healthy Beijing-Seoul relations depend on mutual respect and praised Xi as a “truly reliable neighbor.”\n• China recently conducted military drills around Taiwan.\n• The U.S. planned arms sales to Taiwan, leading to China sanctioning U.S. defense-related companies.\n• Lee stated that Seoul's cooperation with the U.S. does not mean South Korea-China relations should move toward confrontation.\n• Lee said the visit aims to minimize past misunderstandings and elevate South Korea-China relations.\n• South Korea and the U.S. have urged China to use its influence on North Korea to convince it to return to talks or abandon its nuclear program.\n• North Korea launched multiple ballistic missiles on Sunday.\n• Lee's visit aims to strengthen bilateral ties and discuss ways to restore peace on the Korean Peninsula.\n• Lee and Xi will hold talks on security and economic issues.\n• Lee will meet with Zhao Leji and Premier Li Qiang.\n• South Korea will request that China play a constructive role in promoting peace on the Korean Peninsula.\n• South Korea will push for substantial achievements that could directly benefit ordinary citizens in both countries.",
